    category: "Market Intelligence",
    status: "Verified",
    url: "https://agmarknet.gov.in/price-trends-analysis",
    content: "Historical mandi price data across Western India shows peak wheat prices occurring between November and January, while harvest gluts in March-April depress prices by 12-18%. Utilizing e-NAM registered scientific warehouses for short-term storage permits farmers to access Negotiable Warehouse Receipts (NWR) financing while waiting for price recovery.",
    keywords: ["APMC Mandi", "e-NAM", "NWR Loans", "Price Volatility", "Storage"]
